{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-jqpg-j7w6-42pr","cve_id":null,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/security-advisories/GHSA-jqpg-j7w6-42pr","html_url":"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/security/advisories/GHSA-jqpg-j7w6-42pr","summary":"Dynamic record lifting can allocate beyond the hostcall fuel limit","description":"### Impact\r\n\r\nWasmtime's implementation of the dynamically-typed [`Val`] API does not adequately account for the amount of host allocations performed when loading a value from a guest. This means that a guest can return a value which allocates significantly more memory on the host than the host is otherwise keeping track of. This is a hole in the mitigations applied as part of GHSA-852m-cvvp-9p4w and represents a possible denial-of-service vulnerability for hosts.\r\n\r\nThis vulnerability only affects the [`Val`] API of hosts. Hosts that use `bindgen!` and otherwise statically-typed APIs are unaffected by this issue. For hosts using [`Val`] the amount of extra memory that can be allocated on the host depends on the exact shape of the API in question but it can be at least ~100x extra memory, for example.\r\n\r\n### Patches\r\n\r\nWasmtime 36.0.16, 48.0.3, and 49.0.1 have been patched for this issue. \r\n\r\n### Workarounds\r\n\r\nThere is no known workaround to this and users are recommended to upgrade.\r\n\r\n### References\r\n\r\n* [`Val` API][`Val`]\r\n* GHSA-852m-cvvp-9p4w\r\n\r\n[`Val`]: https://docs.rs/wasmtime/latest/wasmtime/component/enum.Val.html","severity":"low","author":null,"publisher":{"login":"cfallin","id":216148,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNjE0OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216148?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cfallin","html_url":"https://github.com/cfallin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cfallin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cfallin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cfallin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cfallin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cfallin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cfallin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cfallin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cfallin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cfallin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-jqpg-j7w6-42pr","type":"GHSA"}],"state":"published","created_at":null,"updated_at":"2026-09-24T19:25:09Z","published_at":"2026-09-24T19:25:09Z","closed_at":null,"withdrawn_at":null,"submission":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"rust","name":"wasmtime"},"vulnerable_version_range":"<= 36.0.15, >= 37.0.0, <= 48.0.2, 49.0.0","patched_versions":"36.0.16, 48.0.3, 49.0.1","vulnerable_functions":[]}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":null,"score":null},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":"CVSS:4.0/AV:A/AC:H/AT:P/PR:L/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","score":1.0}},"cwes":[],"cwe_ids":[],"credits":[{"login":"wilfreddenton","type":"reporter"}],"credits_detailed":[{"user":{"login":"wilfreddenton","id":1426935,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MjY5MzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1426935?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wilfreddenton","html_url":"https://github.com/wilfreddenton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wilfreddenton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wilfreddenton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wilfreddenton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wilfreddenton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wilfreddenton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wilfreddenton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wilfreddenton/repos","events_url":"https://